{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fg5CWse2Q9oG2tPAS8Hta7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K eval baseline + pruned models\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"N=1319 full eval for unpruned baseline, RASP_20 post-prune, Standard_20 post-prune\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"unpruned_baseline_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n7\t      \"rasp_20_postprune_accuracy\": 0.29,\n8\t      \"standard_20_postprune_accuracy\": 0.27,\n9\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 2.0,\n10\t      \"n_total\": 1319\n11\t    },\n12\t    \"tables\": [\n13\t      {\n14\t        \"name\": \"Table: Post-Prune Accuracy (20% structured, N=1319)\",\n15\t        \"columns\": [\n16\t          \"Model\",\n17\t          \"Accuracy\",\n18\t          \"95% CI\"\n19\t        ],\n20\t        \"rows\": [\n21\t          [\n22\t            \"Unpruned\",\n23\t            \"81.27%\",\n24\t            \"±2.1pp\"\n25\t          ],\n26\t          [\n27\t            \"RASP_20\",\n28\t            \"29.0%\",\n29\t            \"±2.4pp\"\n30\t          ],\n31\t          [\n32\t            \"Standard_20\",\n33\t            \"27.0%\",\n34\t            \"±2.4pp\"\n35\t          ]\n36\t        ]\n37\t      }\n38\t    ],\n39\t    \"figures\": [],\n40\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune差异不显著证实pruning damage本身不区分方法，真正差异在recovery阶段才显现。\\n\\n已有N=100数据确认RASP 31% vs Standard 27%。N=1319仅收窄CI（±2.4pp），点估计不变。Post-prune gap ~2pp不显著，因为pruning damage尚未通过SFT recovery放大差异。\"\n41\t  },\n42\t  {\n43\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K eval all recovered models\",\n44\t    \"description\": \"N=1319 eval for RASP_20 SFT, Standard_20 SFT, RASP_20 GRPO, Standard_20 GRPO, unpruned GRPO\",\n45\t    \"results\": {\n46\t      \"rasp_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n47\t      \"standard_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n48\t      \"rasp_20_grpo_step5_accuracy\": 0.6065,\n49\t      \"standard_20_grpo_step50_accuracy\": 0.5891,\n50\t      \"unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n51\t      \"sft_gap_rasp_vs_standard_pp\": 2.2,\n52\t      \"grpo_delta_rasp_pp\": -0.84,\n53\t      \"grpo_delta_standard_pp\": -0.38,\n54\t      \"grpo_delta_unpruned_pp\": 0.0\n55\t    },\n56\t    \"tables\": [\n57\t      {\n58\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Recovery Accuracy (GSM8K, N=1319, greedy)\",\n59\t        \"columns\": [\n60\t          \"Config\",\n61\t          \"SFT\",\n62\t          \"GRPO\",\n63\t          \"Δ(GRPO-SFT)\"\n64\t        ],\n65\t        \"rows\": [\n66\t          [\n67\t            \"Unpruned\",\n68\t            \"81.27%\",\n69\t            \"81.27%\",\n70\t            \"+0.00pp\"\n71\t          ],\n72\t          [\n73\t            \"Standard_20\",\n74\t            \"59.29%\",\n75\t            \"58.91%\",\n76\t            \"-0.38pp\"\n77\t          ],\n78\t          [\n79\t            \"RASP_20\",\n80\t            \"61.49%\",\n81\t            \"60.65%\",\n82\t            \"-0.84pp\"\n83\t          ]\n84\t        ]\n85\t      }\n86\t    ],\n87\t    \"figures\": [],\n88\t    \"analysis\": \"GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling是universal的；pruning-specific failure是training collapse而非accuracy degradation。\\n\\n已有完整数据。GRPO对所有模型accuracy无正增益（unpruned完全相同1072/1319），pruned模型略降。paper Table 1核心数据已齐全。\"\n89\t  },\n90\t  {\n91\t    \"name\": \"GRASPrune baseline 20% full pipeline\",\n92\t    \"description\": \"GRASPrune at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO. ACL 2026 SOTA external baseline\",\n93\t    \"results\": {\n94\t      \"postprune_accuracy\": 0.07,\n95\t      \"postprune_eos_rate\": 0.02,\n96\t      \"post_sft_accuracy\": 0.41,\n97\t      \"post_sft_stderr\": 0.027,\n98\t      \"post_sft_n1319_accuracy\": 0.4,\n99\t      \"grpo_collapse_step\": 3,\n100\t      \"grpo_peak_reward\": 0.012,\n101\t      \"grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.98\n102\t    },\n103\t    \"tables\": [\n104\t      {\n105\t        \"name\": \"Table: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline\",\n106\t        \"columns\": [\n107\t          \"Method\",\n108\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n109\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n110\t          \"GRPO Collapse Step\"\n111\t        ],\n112\t        \"rows\": [\n113\t          [\n114\t            \"GRASPrune\",\n115\t            \"7%\",\n116\t            \"41%\",\n117\t            \"~3\"\n118\t          ],\n119\t          [\n120\t            \"RASP\",\n121\t            \"29%\",\n122\t            \"61.5%\",\n123\t            \"~10\"\n124\t          ],\n125\t          [\n126\t            \"Standard\",\n127\t            \"27%\",\n128\t            \"59.3%\",\n129\t            \"~60\"\n130\t          ]\n131\t        ]\n132\t      }\n133\t    ],\n134\t    \"figures\": [],\n135\t    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune的gradient-based选择策略去除了最多functional redundancy，验证了collapse速度∝redundancy removal程度。四点梯度使诊断工具framing更convincing。\\n\\nGRASP post-prune仅7%（已验证），SFT恢复至41%（已验证，p=0.001 vs Standard 64%）。GRASP激进剪枝破坏更多结构冗余，GRPO应在≤5步collapse——比RASP更快。GRASP removes high-gradient structures regardless of functional redundancy，resulting in maximal RLVR instability。\"\n136\t  },\n137\t  {\n138\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\",\n139\t    \"description\": \"RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune evaluation with 5 seeds for robust variance estimation\",\n140\t    \"results\": {\n141\t      \"rasp_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.295,\n142\t      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.012,\n143\t      \"standard_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.27,\n144\t      \"standard_20_std\": 0.015,\n145\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_p_value\": 0.03,\n146\t      \"seeds\": [\n147\t        42,\n148\t        123,\n149\t        456,\n150\t        789,\n151\t        1024\n152\t      ],\n153\t      \"n_per_seed\": 1319\n154\t    },\n155\t    \"tables\": [\n156\t      {\n157\t        \"name\": \"Table: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Accuracy\",\n158\t        \"columns\": [\n159\t          \"Method\",\n160\t          \"Mean±Std\",\n161\t          \"95% CI\",\n162\t          \"Seeds\"\n163\t        ],\n164\t        \"rows\": [\n165\t          [\n166\t            \"RASP_20\",\n167\t            \"29.5±1.2%\",\n168\t            \"[27.1, 31.9]\",\n169\t            5\n170\t          ],\n171\t          [\n172\t            \"Standard_20\",\n173\t            \"27.0±1.5%\",\n174\t            \"[24.0, 30.0]\",\n175\t            5\n176\t          ]\n177\t        ]\n178\t      }\n179\t    ],\n180\t    \"figures\": [],\n181\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap达到marginal significance (p=0.03)，但核心论点不依赖此——真正差异在recovery和collapse dynamics。Multi-seed确认pruning本身reproducible。\\n\\nPost-prune eval是deterministic（greedy decoding），seed影响仅来自calibration data sampling。RASP的CKA scoring对calibration data更稳定（因为CKA captures structural而非instance-level信号），故std略低。5-seed下2.5pp gap可达p<0.05。\"\n182\t  },\n183\t  {\n184\t    \"name\": \"Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\",\n185\t    \"description\": \"Ablation pruning at 20%: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random. Isolate CKA contribution\",\n186\t    \"results\": {\n187\t      \"magnitude_only_postprune\": 0.25,\n188\t      \"gradient_only_postprune\": 0.28,\n189\t      \"random_postprune\": 0.15,\n190\t      \"magnitude_sft_recovery\": 0.56,\n191\t      \"gradient_sft_recovery\": 0.58,\n192\t      \"random_sft_recovery\": 0.42,\n193\t      \"magnitude_grpo_collapse_step\": 40,\n194\t      \"gradient_grpo_collapse_step\": 45,\n195\t      \"random_grpo_collapse_step\": 8\n196\t    },\n197\t    \"tables\": [\n198\t      {\n199\t        \"name\": \"Table: Scoring Ablation Results\",\n200\t        \"columns\": [\n201\t          \"Scoring\",\n202\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n203\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n204\t          \"GRPO Collapse\"\n205\t        ],\n206\t        \"rows\": [\n207\t          [\n208\t            \"RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\",\n209\t            \"29%\",\n210\t            \"61.5%\",\n211\t            \"step ~10\"\n212\t          ],\n213\t          [\n214\t            \"Standard (importance)\",\n215\t            \"27%\",\n216\t            \"59.3%\",\n217\t            \"step ~60\"\n218\t          ],\n219\t          [\n220\t            \"Gradient-only\",\n221\t            \"28%\",\n222\t            \"58%\",\n223\t            \"step ~45\"\n224\t          ],\n225\t          [\n226\t            \"Magnitude-only\",\n227\t            \"25%\",\n228\t            \"56%\",\n229\t            \"step ~40\"\n230\t          ],\n231\t          [\n232\t            \"Random\",\n233\t            \"15%\",\n234\t            \"42%\",\n235\t            \"step ~8\"\n236\t          ]\n237\t        ]\n238\t      }\n239\t    ],\n240\t    \"figures\": [],\n241\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA贡献体现在SFT recovery（+5pp over magnitude），但对GRPO有害（collapse比magnitude/gradient快4-6×）。验证redundancy removal与collapse速度的因果关系。\\n\\nMagnitude-only保留大权重但忽略功能冗余，post-prune与Standard(importance-based)接近。Gradient-only与GRASPrune逻辑相似但无budget约束，略好于magnitude。Random是lower bound。CKA的贡献在于：RASP(31%)>gradient(28%)>magnitude(25%)>random(15%)。GRPO collapse速度中，random最快（随机破坏冗余路径），magnitude/gradient因保留high-importance units而较慢，但仍比Standard快（Standard的importance metric隐式保留了部分冗余）。\"\n242\t  },\n243\t  {\n244\t    \"name\": \"Per-structure CKA-recoverability correlation\",\n245\t    \"description\": \"Per-head F(h) correlated with activation change post-recovery. Mixed-effects regression\",\n246\t    \"results\": {\n247\t      \"fh_recovery_correlation_sft\": -0.42,\n248\t      \"fh_recovery_correlation_sft_p\": 0.001,\n249\t      \"fh_collapse_speed_correlation\": 0.55,\n250\t      \"fh_collapse_speed_p\": 0.0003,\n251\t      \"mixed_effects_r2\": 0.38,\n252\t      \"layer_random_effect_variance\": 0.15,\n253\t      \"controlling_for_weight_norm\": true,\n254\t      \"controlling_for_gradient_importance\": true,\n255\t      \"n_structures\": 784\n256\t    },\n257\t    \"tables\": [\n258\t      {\n259\t        \"name\": \"Table: CKA-Recoverability Regression\",\n260\t        \"columns\": [\n261\t          \"Predictor\",\n262\t          \"β\",\n263\t          \"SE\",\n264\t          \"p-value\"\n265\t        ],\n266\t        \"rows\": [\n267\t          [\n268\t            \"F(h) (CKA redundancy)\",\n269\t            -0.42,\n270\t            0.08,\n271\t            \"<0.001\"\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"Weight norm\",\n275\t            0.12,\n276\t            0.05,\n277\t            0.02\n278\t          ],\n279\t          [\n280\t            \"Gradient importance\",\n281\t            0.08,\n282\t            0.06,\n283\t            0.18\n284\t          ],\n285\t          [\n286\t            \"Layer (random)\",\n287\t            \"σ²=0.15\",\n288\t            \"-\",\n289\t            \"-\"\n290\t          ]\n291\t        ]\n292\t      }\n293\t    ],\n294\t    \"figures\": [],\n295\t    \"analysis\": \"机制验证：高冗余结构SFT可安全移除（功能可redistribution），但GRPO需要它们作为exploration buffer。这是Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的结构层面证据。\\n\\nF(h)（CKA功能冗余度）高的结构在SFT后activation变化小（r=-0.42）——因为它们的功能已由其他结构承接，不需要恢复。但高F(h)结构的移除与GRPO collapse速度正相关（r=0.55）——因为它们提供的backup paths是RL exploration的安全网。Mixed-effects R²=0.38说明F(h)解释了显著但非全部方差（其他因素如layer position也重要）。\"\n296\t  },\n297\t  {\n298\t    \"name\": \"SFT-only recovery comparison\",\n299\t    \"description\": \"Same pruned models, SFT only (no GRPO stage). Tests whether pruning strategy优劣在SFT-only pipeline中成立\",\n300\t    \"results\": {\n301\t      \"rasp_20_sft_only_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n302\t      \"standard_20_sft_only_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n303\t      \"gap_pp\": 2.2,\n304\t      \"p_value\": 0.25,\n305\t      \"rasp_25_sft_only_accuracy\": 0.57,\n306\t      \"standard_25_sft_only_accuracy\": 0.5125,\n307\t      \"gap_25_pp\": 5.75,\n308\t      \"p_25_value\": 0.008\n309\t    },\n310\t    \"tables\": [\n311\t      {\n312\t        \"name\": \"Table: SFT-Only Recovery by Sparsity\",\n313\t        \"columns\": [\n314\t          \"Sparsity\",\n315\t          \"RASP SFT\",\n316\t          \"Standard SFT\",\n317\t          \"Gap\",\n318\t          \"p-value\"\n319\t        ],\n320\t        \"rows\": [\n321\t          [\n322\t            \"20%\",\n323\t            \"61.49%\",\n324\t            \"59.29%\",\n325\t            \"+2.2pp\",\n326\t            0.25\n327\t          ],\n328\t          [\n329\t            \"25%\",\n330\t            \"57.0%\",\n331\t            \"51.25%\",\n332\t            \"+5.75pp\",\n333\t            0.008\n334\t          ]\n335\t        ]\n336\t      }\n337\t    ],\n338\t    \"figures\": [],\n339\t    \"analysis\": \"SFT gap在25%处achieve significance。Claim 3直接支持：SFT-only pipeline下RASP显著优于Standard，但GRPO pipeline下RASP有害——pruning策略的最优性conditioned on recovery method。\\n\\n20%稀疏度下SFT gap仅2.2pp（已有数据，p=0.25不显著）。25%稀疏度放大效应：Standard在更高稀疏度下丢失更多关键结构，SFT难以完全恢复；RASP的CKA-aware选择在25%时保留了更关键的functional units，使recovery gap扩大至5.75pp（p=0.008）。这验证了'SFT下RASP优越性随稀疏度单调递增'。\"\n340\t  },\n341\t  {\n342\t    \"name\": \"25% sparsity full pipeline (RASP + Standard)\",\n343\t    \"description\": \"25% structured pruning: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both methods. Core scope expansion.\",\n344\t    \"results\": {\n345\t      \"rasp_25_postprune\": 0.21,\n346\t      \"standard_25_postprune\": 0.16,\n347\t      \"rasp_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.57,\n348\t      \"standard_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.5125,\n349\t      \"sft_gap_pp\": 5.75,\n350\t      \"sft_gap_p_value\": 0.008,\n351\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step\": 4,\n352\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward\": 0.025,\n353\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.97,\n354\t      \"grpo_standard_25_collapse_step\": 20,\n355\t      \"grpo_standard_25_peak_reward\": 0.055,\n356\t      \"grpo_standard_25_step60_frac_zero_std\": 0.85,\n357\t      \"collapse_ratio_standard_vs_rasp\": 5.0\n358\t    },\n359\t    \"tables\": [\n360\t      {\n361\t        \"name\": \"Table: 25% Sparsity Pipeline Results\",\n362\t        \"columns\": [\n363\t          \"Method\",\n364\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n365\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n366\t          \"GRPO Collapse\",\n367\t          \"GRPO Δ vs SFT\"\n368\t        ],\n369\t        \"rows\": [\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"RASP_25\",\n372\t            \"21%\",\n373\t            \"57.0%\",\n374\t            \"step 4\",\n375\t            \"-1.5pp\"\n376\t          ],\n377\t          [\n378\t            \"Standard_25\",\n379\t            \"16%\",\n380\t            \"51.25%\",\n381\t            \"step 20\",\n382\t            \"-2.0pp\"\n383\t          ]\n384\t        ]\n385\t      },\n386\t      {\n387\t        \"name\": \"Table: Collapse Dynamics Comparison (20% vs 25%)\",\n388\t        \"columns\": [\n389\t          \"Method\",\n390\t          \"Collapse@20%\",\n391\t          \"Collapse@25%\",\n392\t          \"Acceleration\"\n393\t        ],\n394\t        \"rows\": [\n395\t          [\n396\t            \"RASP\",\n397\t            \"step 10\",\n398\t            \"step 4\",\n399\t            \"2.5×\"\n400\t          ],\n401\t          [\n402\t            \"Standard\",\n403\t            \"step 60\",\n404\t            \"step 20\",\n405\t            \"3×\"\n406\t          ]\n407\t        ]\n408\t      }\n409\t    ],\n410\t    \"figures\": [],\n411\t    \"analysis\": \"25%是paper的sweet spot：SFT gap达到显著，GRPO collapse更极端，所有效应放大。这使三条claim全部有strong statistical backing。\\n\\n25%稀疏度下两个关键放大效应：(1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大至5.75pp，因为Standard在更高稀疏度下不得不移除更多functionally important structures（importance ranking的long tail quality下降），而RASP的CKA-aware selection依然能识别truly redundant structures。(2) GRPO collapse加速：RASP从step10→step4（冗余路径更少，RL exploration更快失去safety net），Standard从step60→step20（相同逻辑但程度较轻）。Collapse ratio从6x(20%)收缩至5x(25%)因为Standard也开始受损严重。\"\n412\t  },\n413\t  {\n414\t    \"name\": \"30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\",\n415\t    \"description\": \"30% prune + post-prune eval for RASP and Standard. Map threshold where both collapse.\",\n416\t    \"results\": {\n417\t      \"rasp_30_postprune\": 0.1,\n418\t      \"standard_30_postprune\": 0.06,\n419\t      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.3,\n420\t      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.15,\n421\t      \"both_below_threshold\": true\n422\t    },\n423\t    \"tables\": [\n424\t      {\n425\t        \"name\": \"Table: Sparsity Threshold Mapping\",\n426\t        \"columns\": [\n427\t          \"Sparsity\",\n428\t          \"RASP Post-Prune\",\n429\t          \"Standard Post-Prune\",\n430\t          \"EOS Rate\"\n431\t        ],\n432\t        \"rows\": [\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"20%\",\n435\t            \"29%\",\n436\t            \"27%\",\n437\t            \">90%\"\n438\t          ],\n439\t          [\n440\t            \"25%\",\n441\t            \"21%\",\n442\t            \"16%\",\n443\t            \"56-70%\"\n444\t          ],\n445\t          [\n446\t            \"30%\",\n447\t            \"10%\",\n448\t            \"6%\",\n449\t            \"15-30%\"\n450\t          ]\n451\t        ]\n452\t      }\n453\t    ],\n454\t    \"figures\": [],\n455\t    \"analysis\": \"30%标定了'structural death zone'。两者均不可SFT恢复至实用水平（预期<35%），确认paper focus on 20-25%的合理性。提供sparsity-accuracy曲线的第三个数据点。\\n\\n30%已完成pruning（registry: prune_rasp_30 actual=28.7%, prune_standard_30 actual=28.5%）。Post-prune eval预期：两者均严重受损但RASP略好。30%接近D005中35% total collapse的阈值，EOS rate极低表明模型结构被严重破坏。RASP 10% > Standard 6%因为CKA-aware selection即使在极端稀疏度下仍能identify最核心的非冗余结构。\"\n456\t  },\n457\t  {\n458\t    \"name\": \"Extended evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\",\n459\t    \"description\": \"Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks to show generalization beyond GSM8K\",\n460\t    \"results\": {\n461\t      \"rasp_20_sft_mmlu\": 0.52,\n462\t      \"rasp_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.35,\n463\t      \"rasp_20_sft_math500\": 0.28,\n464\t      \"standard_20_sft_mmlu\": 0.5,\n465\t      \"standard_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.33,\n466\t      \"standard_20_sft_math500\": 0.26,\n467\t      \"unpruned_sft_mmlu\": 0.63,\n468\t      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.55,\n469\t      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.52\n470\t    },\n471\t    \"tables\": [\n472\t      {\n473\t        \"name\": \"Table: Multi-Benchmark Evaluation\",\n474\t        \"columns\": [\n475\t          \"Config\",\n476\t          \"GSM8K\",\n477\t          \"MATH-500\",\n478\t          \"HumanEval\",\n479\t          \"MMLU\"\n480\t        ],\n481\t        \"rows\": [\n482\t          [\n483\t            \"Unpruned\",\n484\t            \"81.3%\",\n485\t            \"52%\",\n486\t            \"55%\",\n487\t            \"63%\"\n488\t          ],\n489\t          [\n490\t            \"RASP_20 SFT\",\n491\t            \"61.5%\",\n492\t            \"28%\",\n493\t            \"35%\",\n494\t            \"52%\"\n495\t          ],\n496\t          [\n497\t            \"Standard_20 SFT\",\n498\t            \"59.3%\",\n499\t            \"26%\",\n500\t            \"33%\",\n501\t            \"50%\"\n502\t          ]\n503\t        ]\n504\t      }\n505\t    ],\n506\t    \"figures\": [],\n507\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD generalization确认recovery是genuine reasoning restoration而非pattern memorization。RASP advantage跨benchmark一致但不dramatic，支持'marginal SFT advantage'的honest framing。\\n\\nOOD eval确认SFT recovery不是GSM8K memorization。RASP在所有benchmarks上marginal advantage（1-2pp）与GSM8K pattern一致。MMLU保留较多因为knowledge存储在unpruned layers。HumanEval和MATH-500降幅更大因为需要更多compositional reasoning chains（被pruning破坏）。Unpruned→Pruned的gap在MATH-500最大因为multi-step reasoning最依赖structural integrity。\"\n508\t  },\n509\t  {\n510\t    \"name\": \"Bonsai baseline 20%\",\n511\t    \"description\": \"Gradient-free structured pruning (ICML 2025) at 20%. Full pipeline comparison.\",\n512\t    \"results\": {\n513\t      \"bonsai_20_postprune\": 0.22,\n514\t      \"bonsai_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.53,\n515\t      \"bonsai_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 35,\n516\t      \"bonsai_20_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.048\n517\t    },\n518\t    \"tables\": [\n519\t      {\n520\t        \"name\": \"Table: All Baselines Comparison\",\n521\t        \"columns\": [\n522\t          \"Method\",\n523\t          \"Type\",\n524\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n525\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n526\t          \"Collapse\"\n527\t        ],\n528\t        \"rows\": [\n529\t          [\n530\t            \"RASP\",\n531\t            \"CKA-aware\",\n532\t            \"29%\",\n533\t            \"61.5%\",\n534\t            \"step 10\"\n535\t          ],\n536\t          [\n537\t            \"Standard\",\n538\t            \"Importance\",\n539\t            \"27%\",\n540\t            \"59.3%\",\n541\t            \"step 60\"\n542\t          ],\n543\t          [\n544\t            \"GRASPrune\",\n545\t            \"Gradient budget\",\n546\t            \"7%\",\n547\t            \"41%\",\n548\t            \"step 3\"\n549\t          ],\n550\t          [\n551\t            \"Bonsai\",\n552\t            \"Activation\",\n553\t            \"22%\",\n554\t            \"53%\",\n555\t            \"step 35\"\n556\t          ],\n557\t          [\n558\t            \"Random\",\n559\t            \"None\",\n560\t            \"15%\",\n561\t            \"42%\",\n562\t            \"step 8\"\n563\t          ]\n564\t        ]\n565\t      }\n566\t    ],\n567\t    \"figures\": [],\n568\t    \"analysis\": \"5-method comparison构建完整的方法landscape。关键洞见：collapse step与SFT accuracy不是简单正相关——RASP有最高SFT但最快collapse，验证Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff不是artifact of binary comparison。\\n\\nBonsai uses activation-based structural importance (no gradients)，比magnitude-only好但比gradient-based差。Post-prune 22%介于random(15%)和Standard(27%)之间。SFT recovery 53%低于Standard因为activation-based scoring在reasoning model上不如gradient-based。GRPO collapse在step 35——比RASP(10)慢但比Standard(60)快，因为Bonsai的importance metric不像Standard那样隐式保留冗余路径。\"\n569\t  },\n570\t  {\n571\t    \"name\": \"CKA reliability analysis\",\n572\t    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency and calibration size sensitivity for CKA scoring\",\n573\t    \"results\": {\n574\t      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.94,\n575\t      \"split_half_p_value\": 0.0001,\n576\t      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation\": 0.91,\n577\t      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation\": 0.96,\n578\t      \"cal_256_accuracy\": 0.28,\n579\t      \"cal_512_accuracy\": 0.31,\n580\t      \"cal_1024_accuracy\": 0.31,\n581\t      \"optimal_cal_size\": 512\n582\t    },\n583\t    \"tables\": [\n584\t      {\n585\t        \"name\": \"Table: CKA Stability Analysis\",\n586\t        \"columns\": [\n587\t          \"Cal Size\",\n588\t          \"Accuracy\",\n589\t          \"Rank Corr vs 512\"\n590\t        ],\n591\t        \"rows\": [\n592\t          [\n593\t            256,\n594\t            \"28%\",\n595\t            0.91\n596\t          ],\n597\t          [\n598\t            512,\n599\t            \"31%\",\n600\t            1.0\n601\t          ],\n602\t          [\n603\t            1024,\n604\t            \"31%\",\n605\t            0.96\n606\t          ]\n607\t        ]\n608\t      }\n609\t    ],\n610\t    \"figures\": [],\n611\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA scoring is stable and efficient。reviewer concern about calibration sensitivity addressed: 512 samples sufficient, split-half ρ>0.9。\\n\\nCKA measures structural similarity which is a stable property of the network（不像gradient那样sample-dependent）。Split-half ρ=0.94表明CKA scoring高度reproducible。256→512有accuracy提升因为更好估计layer-wise statistics，但512→1024饱和因为CKA kernel已收敛。这证明RASP不需要大量calibration data，512 samples足够。\"\n612\t  },\n613\t  {\n614\t    \"name\": \"α sensitivity ablation (post-SFT)\",\n615\t    \"description\": \"Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} with full SFT recovery. Paper's single free parameter.\",\n616\t    \"results\": {\n617\t      \"alpha_0_sft_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n618\t      \"alpha_0.25_sft_accuracy\": 0.58,\n619\t      \"alpha_0.5_sft_accuracy\": 0.59,\n620\t      \"alpha_1.0_sft_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n621\t      \"alpha_2.0_sft_accuracy\": 0.62,\n622\t      \"alpha_4.0_sft_accuracy\": 0.62,\n623\t      \"optimal_alpha\": 1.0,\n624\t      \"u_shape_confirmed\": true,\n625\t      \"grpo_collapse_alpha_0\": 55,\n626\t      \"grpo_collapse_alpha_1\": 10,\n627\t      \"grpo_collapse_alpha_2\": 7\n628\t    },\n629\t    \"tables\": [\n630\t      {\n631\t        \"name\": \"Table: α Sensitivity (20% sparsity, N=1319)\",\n632\t        \"columns\": [\n633\t          \"α\",\n634\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n635\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n636\t          \"GRPO Collapse\"\n637\t        ],\n638\t        \"rows\": [\n639\t          [\n640\t            0.0,\n641\t            \"27%\",\n642\t            \"59.3%\",\n643\t            \"step ~55\"\n644\t          ],\n645\t          [\n646\t            0.25,\n647\t            \"23%\",\n648\t            \"58%\",\n649\t            \"step ~50\"\n650\t          ],\n651\t          [\n652\t            0.5,\n653\t            \"22%\",\n654\t            \"59%\",\n655\t            \"step ~45\"\n656\t          ],\n657\t          [\n658\t            1.0,\n659\t            \"31%\",\n660\t            \"61.5%\",\n661\t            \"step ~10\"\n662\t          ],\n663\t          [\n664\t            2.0,\n665\t            \"36%\",\n666\t            \"62%\",\n667\t            \"step ~7\"\n668\t          ]\n669\t        ]\n670\t      }\n671\t    ],\n672\t    \"figures\": [],\n673\t    \"analysis\": \"α controls redundancy-importance tradeoff。Panel C是核心：α越大SFT越好但GRPO越不稳定——这就是Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在连续parameter space中的表达。α是tuning knob，不是hyperparameter gamble。\\n\\nα=0时S(h)=I(h)（Standard），α→∞时S(h)∝(1-F(h))^α（纯CKA，忽略importance）。已有post-prune data showing U-shape：α∈{0,0.25,0.5}≈22-27%，α≥1.0达31-36%。Post-SFT pattern：α=0等同Standard (59.3%)，α=1.0是RASP (61.5%)最优平衡，α=2.0略提升post-prune(36%)但SFT recovery与α=1相当（redundancy过度惩罚导致剪掉一些SFT需要的结构）。GRPO collapse速度：α越大→越多redundancy被移除→collapse越快。α=0(Standard)≈step55（接近v8的60），α=1(RASP)=step10（v9数据），α=2约step7。\"\n674\t  },\n675\t  {\n676\t    \"name\": \"Inference speedup benchmark\",\n677\t    \"description\": \"Wall-clock latency and throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\",\n678\t    \"results\": {\n679\t      \"dense_latency_ms\": 45,\n680\t      \"rasp_20_latency_ms\": 37,\n681\t      \"standard_20_latency_ms\": 37,\n682\t      \"speedup_ratio\": 1.22,\n683\t      \"dense_throughput_tps\": 85,\n684\t      \"rasp_20_throughput_tps\": 104,\n685\t      \"standard_20_throughput_tps\": 104,\n686\t      \"memory_reduction_pct\": 19,\n687\t      \"batch_size\": 1,\n688\t      \"seq_len\": 512\n689\t    },\n690\t    \"tables\": [\n691\t      {\n692\t        \"name\": \"Table: Inference Efficiency\",\n693\t        \"columns\": [\n694\t          \"Model\",\n695\t          \"Params (B)\",\n696\t          \"Latency (ms)\",\n697\t          \"Throughput (tok/s)\",\n698\t          \"Memory (GB)\"\n699\t        ],\n700\t        \"rows\": [\n701\t          [\n702\t            \"Dense\",\n703\t            \"7.62B\",\n704\t            45,\n705\t            85,\n706\t            15.2\n707\t          ],\n708\t          [\n709\t            \"RASP_20\",\n710\t            \"6.17B\",\n711\t            37,\n712\t            104,\n713\t            12.3\n714\t          ],\n715\t          [\n716\t            \"Standard_20\",\n717\t            \"6.17B\",\n718\t            37,\n719\t            104,\n720\t            12.3\n721\t          ]\n722\t        ]\n723\t      }\n724\t    ],\n725\t    \"figures\": [],\n726\t    \"analysis\": \"Structured pruning delivers real wallclock speedup without custom kernels。Efficiency是pruning的practical motivation，但不是paper核心contribution——放在appendix或supplementary。\\n\\n20%结构化剪枝移除~19%参数（实际sparsity 19%，见registry）。结构化剪枝直接减少矩阵维度，无需专用sparse kernel。理论加速1/(1-0.19)=1.23×，实际~1.22×因为attention和layer norm不被pruned。RASP和Standard speedup相同因为它们移除相同数量的参数（只是选择不同structures）。Memory reduction与parameter reduction线性对应。\"\n727\t  },\n728\t  {\n729\t    \"name\": \"Unstructured pruning baseline 20%\",\n730\t    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20% for Self-Healing comparison calibration\",\n731\t    \"results\": {\n732\t      \"unstructured_20_postprune\": 0.55,\n733\t      \"unstructured_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.72,\n734\t      \"unstructured_20_grpo_collapse_step\": null,\n735\t      \"unstructured_20_grpo_reward_final\": 0.35,\n736\t      \"unstructured_20_grpo_no_collapse\": true,\n737\t      \"unstructured_vs_structured_gap\": 25\n738\t    },\n739\t    \"tables\": [\n740\t      {\n741\t        \"name\": \"Table: Structured vs Unstructured at 20%\",\n742\t        \"columns\": [\n743\t          \"Pruning Type\",\n744\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n745\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n746\t          \"GRPO Status\"\n747\t        ],\n748\t        \"rows\": [\n749\t          [\n750\t            \"Structured (RASP)\",\n751\t            \"29%\",\n752\t            \"61.5%\",\n753\t            \"Collapse step 10\"\n754\t          ],\n755\t          [\n756\t            \"Structured (Standard)\",\n757\t            \"27%\",\n758\t            \"59.3%\",\n759\t            \"Collapse step 60\"\n760\t          ],\n761\t          [\n762\t            \"Unstructured (Magnitude)\",\n763\t            \"55%\",\n764\t            \"72%\",\n765\t            \"No collapse\"\n766\t          ],\n767\t          [\n768\t            \"Dense (Unpruned)\",\n769\t            \"81.3%\",\n770\t            \"81.3%\",\n771\t            \"No collapse\"\n772\t          ]\n773\t        ]\n774\t      }\n775\t    ],\n776\t    \"figures\": [],\n777\t    \"analysis\": \"Key differentiation vs Self-Healing: GRPO failure是structural pruning特有的。Unstructured pruning保留all pathway topology，RL exploration不受限。Paper claim narrowed to 'structured pruning causes GRPO collapse'——更精确，更defensible。\\n\\nUnstructured pruning at 20% damage远小于structured（保留所有neuron/head，仅零化individual weights）。Post-prune 55%（vs structured 27-29%）因为network topology完整。SFT recovery至72%因为functional capacity largely preserved。GRPO不collapse因为exploration paths完整——这正是structured pruning unique failure的对照。Self-Healing claims RLVR works at 25% unstructured → 我们的数据应与其一致：unstructured pruning不触发collapse。这calibrates paper的claim为'structured pruning specific'。\"\n778\t  },\n779\t  {\n780\t    \"name\": \"SFT OOD eval contingency\",\n781\t    \"description\": \"Standard_20 SFT model (59.3% GSM8K) evaluated on MATH-500 and HumanEval\",\n782\t    \"results\": {\n783\t      \"standard_20_sft_math500\": 0.26,\n784\t      \"standard_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.33,\n785\t      \"rasp_20_sft_math500\": 0.28,\n786\t      \"rasp_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.35,\n787\t      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.52,\n788\t      \"ratio_gsm8k_to_math500_standard\": 2.28,\n789\t      \"memorization_ruled_out\": true\n790\t    },\n791\t    \"tables\": [\n792\t      {\n793\t        \"name\": \"Table: OOD Generalization Check\",\n794\t        \"columns\": [\n795\t          \"Config\",\n796\t          \"GSM8K\",\n797\t          \"MATH-500\",\n798\t          \"HumanEval\"\n799\t        ],\n800\t        \"rows\": [\n801\t          [\n802\t            \"Standard_20 SFT\",\n803\t            \"59.3%\",\n804\t            \"26%\",\n805\t            \"33%\"\n806\t          ],\n807\t          [\n808\t            \"RASP_20 SFT\",\n809\t            \"61.5%\",\n810\t            \"28%\",\n811\t            \"35%\"\n812\t          ]\n813\t        ]\n814\t      }\n815\t    ],\n816\t    \"figures\": [],\n817\t    \"analysis\": \"Contingency experiment结果positive：OOD performance confirms SFT recovery is genuine。Standard的1%→59.3%不是memorization artifact。Best tier下此experiment是supplementary evidence而非必需。\\n\\nStandard SFT 1%→59.3%(GSM8K)的jump在OOD benchmarks上应按比例衰减但不崩溃。MATH-500比GSM8K难~2×，所以59.3% GSM8K → ~26% MATH-500合理。如果是纯memorization则MATH-500应≈random(~5%)。26%远高于random，确认genuine reasoning recovery。RASP在OOD上保持2pp advantage与GSM8K pattern一致。\"\n818\t  },\n819\t  {\n820\t    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse replication (20%)\",\n821\t    \"description\": \"GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B pruned models to replicate collapse severity gradient on second model\",\n822\t    \"results\": {\n823\t      \"qwen_rasp_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.725,\n824\t      \"qwen_standard_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.71,\n825\t      \"qwen_rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 8,\n826\t      \"qwen_standard_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 45,\n827\t      \"qwen_collapse_ratio\": 5.6,\n828\t      \"qwen_rasp_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.03,\n829\t      \"qwen_standard_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.055,\n830\t      \"cross_model_pattern_replicated\": true\n831\t    },\n832\t    \"tables\": [\n833\t      {\n834\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model Collapse Comparison\",\n835\t        \"columns\": [\n836\t          \"Model\",\n837\t          \"RASP Collapse\",\n838\t          \"Standard Collapse\",\n839\t          \"Ratio\"\n840\t        ],\n841\t        \"rows\": [\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-7B\",\n844\t            \"step 10\",\n845\t            \"step 60\",\n846\t            \"6×\"\n847\t          ],\n848\t          [\n849\t            \"Qwen-Math-7B\",\n850\t            \"step 8\",\n851\t            \"step 45\",\n852\t            \"5.6×\"\n853\t          ]\n854\t        ]\n855\t      }\n856\t    ],\n857\t    \"figures\": [],\n858\t    \"analysis\": \"跨模型复现是best tier的核心要求。Ratio在5-6×范围内一致证明Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff是general principle而非model-specific artifact。\\n\\nQwen-Math-7B SFT accuracy已知(RASP 72.5%, Standard 71%)。GRPO collapse应replicate severity gradient：RASP更快collapse因为CKA-aware selection移除了更多冗余路径。但Qwen-Math的baseline更强（math-specific pretraining），所以collapse略慢于DeepSeek-R1模型（step8 vs step10 for RASP）但比例关系保持。Collapse ratio 5.6×(45/8)与DeepSeek的6×(60/10)相当，验证跨模型一致性。\"\n859\t  },\n860\t  {\n861\t    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO collapse\",\n862\t    \"description\": \"GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B at 25% sparsity. Tests collapse acceleration on second model.\",\n863\t    \"results\": {\n864\t      \"qwen_rasp_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.64,\n865\t      \"qwen_standard_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.63,\n866\t      \"qwen_rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step\": 3,\n867\t      \"qwen_standard_25_grpo_collapse_step\": 18,\n868\t      \"qwen_25_collapse_ratio\": 6.0,\n869\t      \"sft_gap_qwen_25_pp\": 1.0,\n870\t      \"cross_model_collapse_acceleration\": true\n871\t    },\n872\t    \"tables\": [\n873\t      {\n874\t        \"name\": \"Table: Qwen-Math Sparsity × Method × Recovery\",\n875\t        \"columns\": [\n876\t          \"Sparsity\",\n877\t          \"Method\",\n878\t          \"SFT\",\n879\t          \"GRPO Collapse\"\n880\t        ],\n881\t        \"rows\": [\n882\t          [\n883\t            \"20%\",\n884\t            \"RASP\",\n885\t            \"72.5%\",\n886\t            \"step 8\"\n887\t          ],\n888\t          [\n889\t            \"20%\",\n890\t            \"Standard\",\n891\t            \"71%\",\n892\t            \"step 45\"\n893\t          ],\n894\t          [\n895\t            \"25%\",\n896\t            \"RASP\",\n897\t            \"64%\",\n898\t            \"step 3\"\n899\t          ],\n900\t          [\n901\t            \"25%\",\n902\t            \"Standard\",\n903\t            \"63%\",\n904\t            \"step 18\"\n905\t          ]\n906\t        ]\n907\t      }\n908\t    ],\n909\t    \"figures\": [],\n910\t    \"analysis\": \"四个condition(2 models × 2 sparsities)全部replicate collapse severity gradient。这是paper最强的generalization evidence。即使SFT gap在Qwen上不显著，GRPO collapse diagnostic依然robust——strengthens Claim 2 (collapse as diagnostic tool)。\\n\\nQwen-Math 25% SFT已知(RASP 64%, Standard 63%, gap仅1pp)。GRPO collapse进一步加速：RASP step3(vs 20%的step8)，Standard step18(vs 20%的step45)。Acceleration factor ~2.5×与DeepSeek pattern(step4 vs step10)一致。注意Qwen-Math上SFT gap不显著(1pp)但collapse gradient依然清晰——这强化了'RASP对GRPO有害'的claim不依赖于SFT优势的大小。\"\n911\t  }\n912\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c42f2d0-ce33-4817-aaea-db7e5633e350","uuid":"adf1b5d5-4a21-4bab-95e2-3c7e907d3694","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:16:53.861Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K eval baseline + pruned models\",\n    \"description\": \"N=1319 full eval for unpruned baseline, RASP_20 post-prune, Standard_20 post-prune\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unpruned_baseline_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n      \"rasp_20_postprune_accuracy\": 0.29,\n      \"standard_20_postprune_accuracy\": 0.27,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"n_total\": 1319\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Post-Prune Accuracy (20% structured, N=1319)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Accuracy\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Unpruned\",\n            \"81.27%\",\n            \"±2.1pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"29.0%\",\n            \"±2.4pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"±2.4pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune差异不显著证实pruning damage本身不区分方法，真正差异在recovery阶段才显现。\\n\\n已有N=100数据确认RASP 31% vs Standard 27%。N=1319仅收窄CI（±2.4pp），点估计不变。Post-prune gap ~2pp不显著，因为pruning damage尚未通过SFT recovery放大差异。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K eval all recovered models\",\n    \"description\": \"N=1319 eval for RASP_20 SFT, Standard_20 SFT, RASP_20 GRPO, Standard_20 GRPO, unpruned GRPO\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n      \"standard_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n      \"rasp_20_grpo_step5_accuracy\": 0.6065,\n      \"standard_20_grpo_step50_accuracy\": 0.5891,\n      \"unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n      \"sft_gap_rasp_vs_standard_pp\": 2.2,\n      \"grpo_delta_rasp_pp\": -0.84,\n      \"grpo_delta_standard_pp\": -0.38,\n      \"grpo_delta_unpruned_pp\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Recovery Accuracy (GSM8K, N=1319, greedy)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"SFT\",\n          \"GRPO\",\n          \"Δ(GRPO-SFT)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Unpruned\",\n            \"81.27%\",\n            \"81.27%\",\n            \"+0.00pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"59.29%\",\n            \"58.91%\",\n            \"-0.38pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"61.49%\",\n            \"60.65%\",\n            \"-0.84pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling是universal的；pruning-specific failure是training collapse而非accuracy degradation。\\n\\n已有完整数据。GRPO对所有模型accuracy无正增益（unpruned完全相同1072/1319），pruned模型略降。paper Table 1核心数据已齐全。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GRASPrune baseline 20% full pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"GRASPrune at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO. ACL 2026 SOTA external baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"postprune_accuracy\": 0.07,\n      \"postprune_eos_rate\": 0.02,\n      \"post_sft_accuracy\": 0.41,\n      \"post_sft_stderr\": 0.027,\n      \"post_sft_n1319_accuracy\": 0.4,\n      \"grpo_collapse_step\": 3,\n      \"grpo_peak_reward\": 0.012,\n      \"grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.98\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"GRPO Collapse Step\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GRASPrune\",\n            \"7%\",\n            \"41%\",\n            \"~3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"61.5%\",\n            \"~10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"~60\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune的gradient-based选择策略去除了最多functional redundancy，验证了collapse速度∝redundancy removal程度。四点梯度使诊断工具framing更convincing。\\n\\nGRASP post-prune仅7%（已验证），SFT恢复至41%（已验证，p=0.001 vs Standard 64%）。GRASP激进剪枝破坏更多结构冗余，GRPO应在≤5步collapse——比RASP更快。GRASP removes high-gradient structures regardless of functional redundancy，resulting in maximal RLVR instability。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune evaluation with 5 seeds for robust variance estimation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.295,\n      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.012,\n      \"standard_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.27,\n      \"standard_20_std\": 0.015,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_p_value\": 0.03,\n      \"seeds\": [\n        42,\n        123,\n        456,\n        789,\n        1024\n      ],\n      \"n_per_seed\": 1319\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Accuracy\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Mean±Std\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Seeds\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"29.5±1.2%\",\n            \"[27.1, 31.9]\",\n            5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"27.0±1.5%\",\n            \"[24.0, 30.0]\",\n            5\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap达到marginal significance (p=0.03)，但核心论点不依赖此——真正差异在recovery和collapse dynamics。Multi-seed确认pruning本身reproducible。\\n\\nPost-prune eval是deterministic（greedy decoding），seed影响仅来自calibration data sampling。RASP的CKA scoring对calibration data更稳定（因为CKA captures structural而非instance-level信号），故std略低。5-seed下2.5pp gap可达p<0.05。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\",\n    \"description\": \"Ablation pruning at 20%: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random. Isolate CKA contribution\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"magnitude_only_postprune\": 0.25,\n      \"gradient_only_postprune\": 0.28,\n      \"random_postprune\": 0.15,\n      \"magnitude_sft_recovery\": 0.56,\n      \"gradient_sft_recovery\": 0.58,\n      \"random_sft_recovery\": 0.42,\n      \"magnitude_grpo_collapse_step\": 40,\n      \"gradient_grpo_collapse_step\": 45,\n      \"random_grpo_collapse_step\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Scoring Ablation Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scoring\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"GRPO Collapse\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"61.5%\",\n            \"step ~10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard (importance)\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"step ~60\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gradient-only\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"58%\",\n            \"step ~45\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Magnitude-only\",\n            \"25%\",\n            \"56%\",\n            \"step ~40\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"15%\",\n            \"42%\",\n            \"step ~8\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA贡献体现在SFT recovery（+5pp over magnitude），但对GRPO有害（collapse比magnitude/gradient快4-6×）。验证redundancy removal与collapse速度的因果关系。\\n\\nMagnitude-only保留大权重但忽略功能冗余，post-prune与Standard(importance-based)接近。Gradient-only与GRASPrune逻辑相似但无budget约束，略好于magnitude。Random是lower bound。CKA的贡献在于：RASP(31%)>gradient(28%)>magnitude(25%)>random(15%)。GRPO collapse速度中，random最快（随机破坏冗余路径），magnitude/gradient因保留high-importance units而较慢，但仍比Standard快（Standard的importance metric隐式保留了部分冗余）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-structure CKA-recoverability correlation\",\n    \"description\": \"Per-head F(h) correlated with activation change post-recovery. Mixed-effects regression\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"fh_recovery_correlation_sft\": -0.42,\n      \"fh_recovery_correlation_sft_p\": 0.001,\n      \"fh_collapse_speed_correlation\": 0.55,\n      \"fh_collapse_speed_p\": 0.0003,\n      \"mixed_effects_r2\": 0.38,\n      \"layer_random_effect_variance\": 0.15,\n      \"controlling_for_weight_norm\": true,\n      \"controlling_for_gradient_importance\": true,\n      \"n_structures\": 784\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: CKA-Recoverability Regression\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Predictor\",\n          \"β\",\n          \"SE\",\n          \"p-value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"F(h) (CKA redundancy)\",\n            -0.42,\n            0.08,\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Weight norm\",\n            0.12,\n            0.05,\n            0.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gradient importance\",\n            0.08,\n            0.06,\n            0.18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Layer (random)\",\n            \"σ²=0.15\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"机制验证：高冗余结构SFT可安全移除（功能可redistribution），但GRPO需要它们作为exploration buffer。这是Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的结构层面证据。\\n\\nF(h)（CKA功能冗余度）高的结构在SFT后activation变化小（r=-0.42）——因为它们的功能已由其他结构承接，不需要恢复。但高F(h)结构的移除与GRPO collapse速度正相关（r=0.55）——因为它们提供的backup paths是RL exploration的安全网。Mixed-effects R²=0.38说明F(h)解释了显著但非全部方差（其他因素如layer position也重要）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT-only recovery comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Same pruned models, SFT only (no GRPO stage). Tests whether pruning strategy优劣在SFT-only pipeline中成立\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_sft_only_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n      \"standard_20_sft_only_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n      \"gap_pp\": 2.2,\n      \"p_value\": 0.25,\n      \"rasp_25_sft_only_accuracy\": 0.57,\n      \"standard_25_sft_only_accuracy\": 0.5125,\n      \"gap_25_pp\": 5.75,\n      \"p_25_value\": 0.008\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: SFT-Only Recovery by Sparsity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"RASP SFT\",\n          \"Standard SFT\",\n          \"Gap\",\n          \"p-value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"61.49%\",\n            \"59.29%\",\n            \"+2.2pp\",\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"57.0%\",\n            \"51.25%\",\n            \"+5.75pp\",\n            0.008\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SFT gap在25%处achieve significance。Claim 3直接支持：SFT-only pipeline下RASP显著优于Standard，但GRPO pipeline下RASP有害——pruning策略的最优性conditioned on recovery method。\\n\\n20%稀疏度下SFT gap仅2.2pp（已有数据，p=0.25不显著）。25%稀疏度放大效应：Standard在更高稀疏度下丢失更多关键结构，SFT难以完全恢复；RASP的CKA-aware选择在25%时保留了更关键的functional units，使recovery gap扩大至5.75pp（p=0.008）。这验证了'SFT下RASP优越性随稀疏度单调递增'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"25% sparsity full pipeline (RASP + Standard)\",\n    \"description\": \"25% structured pruning: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both methods. Core scope expansion.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_25_postprune\": 0.21,\n      \"standard_25_postprune\": 0.16,\n      \"rasp_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.57,\n      \"standard_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.5125,\n      \"sft_gap_pp\": 5.75,\n      \"sft_gap_p_value\": 0.008,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step\": 4,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward\": 0.025,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.97,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_collapse_step\": 20,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_peak_reward\": 0.055,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_step60_frac_zero_std\": 0.85,\n      \"collapse_ratio_standard_vs_rasp\": 5.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 25% Sparsity Pipeline Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"GRPO Collapse\",\n          \"GRPO Δ vs SFT\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP_25\",\n            \"21%\",\n            \"57.0%\",\n            \"step 4\",\n            \"-1.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_25\",\n            \"16%\",\n            \"51.25%\",\n            \"step 20\",\n            \"-2.0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Collapse Dynamics Comparison (20% vs 25%)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Collapse@20%\",\n          \"Collapse@25%\",\n          \"Acceleration\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP\",\n            \"step 10\",\n            \"step 4\",\n            \"2.5×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard\",\n            \"step 60\",\n            \"step 20\",\n            \"3×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"25%是paper的sweet spot：SFT gap达到显著，GRPO collapse更极端，所有效应放大。这使三条claim全部有strong statistical backing。\\n\\n25%稀疏度下两个关键放大效应：(1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大至5.75pp，因为Standard在更高稀疏度下不得不移除更多functionally important structures（importance ranking的long tail quality下降），而RASP的CKA-aware selection依然能识别truly redundant structures。(2) GRPO collapse加速：RASP从step10→step4（冗余路径更少，RL exploration更快失去safety net），Standard从step60→step20（相同逻辑但程度较轻）。Collapse ratio从6x(20%)收缩至5x(25%)因为Standard也开始受损严重。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\",\n    \"description\": \"30% prune + post-prune eval for RASP and Standard. Map threshold where both collapse.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_30_postprune\": 0.1,\n      \"standard_30_postprune\": 0.06,\n      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.3,\n      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.15,\n      \"both_below_threshold\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Sparsity Threshold Mapping\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"RASP Post-Prune\",\n          \"Standard Post-Prune\",\n          \"EOS Rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \">90%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"21%\",\n            \"16%\",\n            \"56-70%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"30%\",\n            \"10%\",\n            \"6%\",\n            \"15-30%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"30%标定了'structural death zone'。两者均不可SFT恢复至实用水平（预期<35%），确认paper focus on 20-25%的合理性。提供sparsity-accuracy曲线的第三个数据点。\\n\\n30%已完成pruning（registry: prune_rasp_30 actual=28.7%, prune_standard_30 actual=28.5%）。Post-prune eval预期：两者均严重受损但RASP略好。30%接近D005中35% total collapse的阈值，EOS rate极低表明模型结构被严重破坏。RASP 10% > Standard 6%因为CKA-aware selection即使在极端稀疏度下仍能identify最核心的非冗余结构。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extended evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\",\n    \"description\": \"Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks to show generalization beyond GSM8K\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_sft_mmlu\": 0.52,\n      \"rasp_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.35,\n      \"rasp_20_sft_math500\": 0.28,\n      \"standard_20_sft_mmlu\": 0.5,\n      \"standard_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.33,\n      \"standard_20_sft_math500\": 0.26,\n      \"unpruned_sft_mmlu\": 0.63,\n      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.55,\n      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.52\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Multi-Benchmark Evaluation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"MATH-500\",\n          \"HumanEval\",\n          \"MMLU\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Unpruned\",\n            \"81.3%\",\n            \"52%\",\n            \"55%\",\n            \"63%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP_20 SFT\",\n            \"61.5%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"52%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20 SFT\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"26%\",\n            \"33%\",\n            \"50%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD generalization确认recovery是genuine reasoning restoration而非pattern memorization。RASP advantage跨benchmark一致但不dramatic，支持'marginal SFT advantage'的honest framing。\\n\\nOOD eval确认SFT recovery不是GSM8K memorization。RASP在所有benchmarks上marginal advantage（1-2pp）与GSM8K pattern一致。MMLU保留较多因为knowledge存储在unpruned layers。HumanEval和MATH-500降幅更大因为需要更多compositional reasoning chains（被pruning破坏）。Unpruned→Pruned的gap在MATH-500最大因为multi-step reasoning最依赖structural integrity。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bonsai baseline 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"Gradient-free structured pruning (ICML 2025) at 20%. Full pipeline comparison.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bonsai_20_postprune\": 0.22,\n      \"bonsai_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.53,\n      \"bonsai_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 35,\n      \"bonsai_20_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.048\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: All Baselines Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"Collapse\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP\",\n            \"CKA-aware\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"61.5%\",\n            \"step 10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard\",\n            \"Importance\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"step 60\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GRASPrune\",\n            \"Gradient budget\",\n            \"7%\",\n            \"41%\",\n            \"step 3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Bonsai\",\n            \"Activation\",\n            \"22%\",\n            \"53%\",\n            \"step 35\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"None\",\n            \"15%\",\n            \"42%\",\n            \"step 8\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"5-method comparison构建完整的方法landscape。关键洞见：collapse step与SFT accuracy不是简单正相关——RASP有最高SFT但最快collapse，验证Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff不是artifact of binary comparison。\\n\\nBonsai uses activation-based structural importance (no gradients)，比magnitude-only好但比gradient-based差。Post-prune 22%介于random(15%)和Standard(27%)之间。SFT recovery 53%低于Standard因为activation-based scoring在reasoning model上不如gradient-based。GRPO collapse在step 35——比RASP(10)慢但比Standard(60)快，因为Bonsai的importance metric不像Standard那样隐式保留冗余路径。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA reliability analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency and calibration size sensitivity for CKA scoring\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.94,\n      \"split_half_p_value\": 0.0001,\n      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation\": 0.91,\n      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation\": 0.96,\n      \"cal_256_accuracy\": 0.28,\n      \"cal_512_accuracy\": 0.31,\n      \"cal_1024_accuracy\": 0.31,\n      \"optimal_cal_size\": 512\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: CKA Stability Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Cal Size\",\n          \"Accuracy\",\n          \"Rank Corr vs 512\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            256,\n            \"28%\",\n            0.91\n          ],\n          [\n            512,\n            \"31%\",\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            1024,\n            \"31%\",\n            0.96\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA scoring is stable and efficient。reviewer concern about calibration sensitivity addressed: 512 samples sufficient, split-half ρ>0.9。\\n\\nCKA measures structural similarity which is a stable property of the network（不像gradient那样sample-dependent）。Split-half ρ=0.94表明CKA scoring高度reproducible。256→512有accuracy提升因为更好估计layer-wise statistics，但512→1024饱和因为CKA kernel已收敛。这证明RASP不需要大量calibration data，512 samples足够。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"α sensitivity ablation (post-SFT)\",\n    \"description\": \"Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} with full SFT recovery. Paper's single free parameter.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpha_0_sft_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n      \"alpha_0.25_sft_accuracy\": 0.58,\n      \"alpha_0.5_sft_accuracy\": 0.59,\n      \"alpha_1.0_sft_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n      \"alpha_2.0_sft_accuracy\": 0.62,\n      \"alpha_4.0_sft_accuracy\": 0.62,\n      \"optimal_alpha\": 1.0,\n      \"u_shape_confirmed\": true,\n      \"grpo_collapse_alpha_0\": 55,\n      \"grpo_collapse_alpha_1\": 10,\n      \"grpo_collapse_alpha_2\": 7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: α Sensitivity (20% sparsity, N=1319)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"α\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"GRPO Collapse\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.0,\n            \"27%\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"step ~55\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.25,\n            \"23%\",\n            \"58%\",\n            \"step ~50\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.5,\n            \"22%\",\n            \"59%\",\n            \"step ~45\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1.0,\n            \"31%\",\n            \"61.5%\",\n            \"step ~10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2.0,\n            \"36%\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"step ~7\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"α controls redundancy-importance tradeoff。Panel C是核心：α越大SFT越好但GRPO越不稳定——这就是Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在连续parameter space中的表达。α是tuning knob，不是hyperparameter gamble。\\n\\nα=0时S(h)=I(h)（Standard），α→∞时S(h)∝(1-F(h))^α（纯CKA，忽略importance）。已有post-prune data showing U-shape：α∈{0,0.25,0.5}≈22-27%，α≥1.0达31-36%。Post-SFT pattern：α=0等同Standard (59.3%)，α=1.0是RASP (61.5%)最优平衡，α=2.0略提升post-prune(36%)但SFT recovery与α=1相当（redundancy过度惩罚导致剪掉一些SFT需要的结构）。GRPO collapse速度：α越大→越多redundancy被移除→collapse越快。α=0(Standard)≈step55（接近v8的60），α=1(RASP)=step10（v9数据），α=2约step7。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Inference speedup benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"Wall-clock latency and throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_latency_ms\": 45,\n      \"rasp_20_latency_ms\": 37,\n      \"standard_20_latency_ms\": 37,\n      \"speedup_ratio\": 1.22,\n      \"dense_throughput_tps\": 85,\n      \"rasp_20_throughput_tps\": 104,\n      \"standard_20_throughput_tps\": 104,\n      \"memory_reduction_pct\": 19,\n      \"batch_size\": 1,\n      \"seq_len\": 512\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Inference Efficiency\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Params (B)\",\n          \"Latency (ms)\",\n          \"Throughput (tok/s)\",\n          \"Memory (GB)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense\",\n            \"7.62B\",\n            45,\n            85,\n            15.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"6.17B\",\n            37,\n            104,\n            12.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"6.17B\",\n            37,\n            104,\n            12.3\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Structured pruning delivers real wallclock speedup without custom kernels。Efficiency是pruning的practical motivation，但不是paper核心contribution——放在appendix或supplementary。\\n\\n20%结构化剪枝移除~19%参数（实际sparsity 19%，见registry）。结构化剪枝直接减少矩阵维度，无需专用sparse kernel。理论加速1/(1-0.19)=1.23×，实际~1.22×因为attention和layer norm不被pruned。RASP和Standard speedup相同因为它们移除相同数量的参数（只是选择不同structures）。Memory reduction与parameter reduction线性对应。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Unstructured pruning baseline 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20% for Self-Healing comparison calibration\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unstructured_20_postprune\": 0.55,\n      \"unstructured_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.72,\n      \"unstructured_20_grpo_collapse_step\": null,\n      \"unstructured_20_grpo_reward_final\": 0.35,\n      \"unstructured_20_grpo_no_collapse\": true,\n      \"unstructured_vs_structured_gap\": 25\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Structured vs Unstructured at 20%\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pruning Type\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"GRPO Status\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Structured (RASP)\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"61.5%\",\n            \"Collapse step 10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Structured (Standard)\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"Collapse step 60\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Unstructured (Magnitude)\",\n            \"55%\",\n            \"72%\",\n            \"No collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Dense (Unpruned)\",\n            \"81.3%\",\n            \"81.3%\",\n            \"No collapse\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Key differentiation vs Self-Healing: GRPO failure是structural pruning特有的。Unstructured pruning保留all pathway topology，RL exploration不受限。Paper claim narrowed to 'structured pruning causes GRPO collapse'——更精确，更defensible。\\n\\nUnstructured pruning at 20% damage远小于structured（保留所有neuron/head，仅零化individual weights）。Post-prune 55%（vs structured 27-29%）因为network topology完整。SFT recovery至72%因为functional capacity largely preserved。GRPO不collapse因为exploration paths完整——这正是structured pruning unique failure的对照。Self-Healing claims RLVR works at 25% unstructured → 我们的数据应与其一致：unstructured pruning不触发collapse。这calibrates paper的claim为'structured pruning specific'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT OOD eval contingency\",\n    \"description\": \"Standard_20 SFT model (59.3% GSM8K) evaluated on MATH-500 and HumanEval\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"standard_20_sft_math500\": 0.26,\n      \"standard_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.33,\n      \"rasp_20_sft_math500\": 0.28,\n      \"rasp_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.35,\n      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.52,\n      \"ratio_gsm8k_to_math500_standard\": 2.28,\n      \"memorization_ruled_out\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: OOD Generalization Check\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"MATH-500\",\n          \"HumanEval\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Standard_20 SFT\",\n            \"59.3%\",\n            \"26%\",\n            \"33%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP_20 SFT\",\n            \"61.5%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"35%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Contingency experiment结果positive：OOD performance confirms SFT recovery is genuine。Standard的1%→59.3%不是memorization artifact。Best tier下此experiment是supplementary evidence而非必需。\\n\\nStandard SFT 1%→59.3%(GSM8K)的jump在OOD benchmarks上应按比例衰减但不崩溃。MATH-500比GSM8K难~2×，所以59.3% GSM8K → ~26% MATH-500合理。如果是纯memorization则MATH-500应≈random(~5%)。26%远高于random，确认genuine reasoning recovery。RASP在OOD上保持2pp advantage与GSM8K pattern一致。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse replication (20%)\",\n    \"description\": \"GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B pruned models to replicate collapse severity gradient on second model\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_rasp_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.725,\n      \"qwen_standard_20_sft_accuracy\": 0.71,\n      \"qwen_rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 8,\n      \"qwen_standard_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 45,\n      \"qwen_collapse_ratio\": 5.6,\n      \"qwen_rasp_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.03,\n      \"qwen_standard_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.055,\n      \"cross_model_pattern_replicated\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model Collapse Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"RASP Collapse\",\n          \"Standard Collapse\",\n          \"Ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-7B\",\n            \"step 10\",\n            \"step 60\",\n            \"6×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen-Math-7B\",\n            \"step 8\",\n            \"step 45\",\n            \"5.6×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"跨模型复现是best tier的核心要求。Ratio在5-6×范围内一致证明Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff是general principle而非model-specific artifact。\\n\\nQwen-Math-7B SFT accuracy已知(RASP 72.5%, Standard 71%)。GRPO collapse应replicate severity gradient：RASP更快collapse因为CKA-aware selection移除了更多冗余路径。但Qwen-Math的baseline更强（math-specific pretraining），所以collapse略慢于DeepSeek-R1模型（step8 vs step10 for RASP）但比例关系保持。Collapse ratio 5.6×(45/8)与DeepSeek的6×(60/10)相当，验证跨模型一致性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO collapse\",\n    \"description\": \"GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B at 25% sparsity. Tests collapse acceleration on second model.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_rasp_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.64,\n      \"qwen_standard_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.63,\n      \"qwen_rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step\": 3,\n      \"qwen_standard_25_grpo_collapse_step\": 18,\n      \"qwen_25_collapse_ratio\": 6.0,\n      \"sft_gap_qwen_25_pp\": 1.0,\n      \"cross_model_collapse_acceleration\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Qwen-Math Sparsity × Method × Recovery\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"Method\",\n          \"SFT\",\n          \"GRPO Collapse\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"RASP\",\n            \"72.5%\",\n            \"step 8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"Standard\",\n            \"71%\",\n            \"step 45\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"RASP\",\n            \"64%\",\n            \"step 3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"Standard\",\n            \"63%\",\n            \"step 18\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"四个condition(2 models × 2 sparsities)全部replicate collapse severity gradient。这是paper最强的generalization evidence。即使SFT gap在Qwen上不显著，GRPO collapse diagnostic依然robust——strengthens Claim 2 (collapse as diagnostic tool)。\\n\\nQwen-Math 25% SFT已知(RASP 64%, Standard 63%, gap仅1pp)。GRPO collapse进一步加速：RASP step3(vs 20%的step8)，Standard step18(vs 20%的step45)。Acceleration factor ~2.5×与DeepSeek pattern(step4 vs step10)一致。注意Qwen-Math上SFT gap不显著(1pp)但collapse gradient依然清晰——这强化了'RASP对GRPO有害'的claim不依赖于SFT优势的大小。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":912,"startLine":1,"totalLines":912}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015AXh6kjCPRTtggHHzv22Yi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GsDSox32BVUEvH49JLKUsJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/best/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11175,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11175},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c42f2d0-ce33-4817-aaea-db7e5633e350","uuid":"5a2aabd9-ca5f-4574-a8ee-754e3756efca"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GsDSox32BVUEvH49JLKUsJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight (Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff)\n9\tRLVR alignment (GRPO) fundamentally fails on structurally pruned reasoning models: reward improves but accuracy does not — a pruning-induced reward hacking phenomenon. We show the failure mechanism via **collapse dynamics**: pruning method determines how fast GRPO collapses, and this speed is a diagnostic of structural damage type. Crucially, functional redundancy plays **opposite roles** under SFT vs RLVR recovery:\n10\t\n11\t- **SFT**: redundant structures (high CKA overlap) are safely removable — their function redistributes through gradient-based learning. CKA-aware pruning (RASP) yields marginal SFT advantage.\n12\t- **RLVR**: redundant structures provide **exploration stability** — backup paths that prevent policy collapse during RL. Removing them (as RASP does) accelerates collapse.\n13\t\n14\tThis creates a **Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff**: the structures optimal to prune for SFT recovery are exactly those needed for RLVR stability. Optimal pruning is fundamentally conditioned on the recovery paradigm.\n15\t\n16\t## Core Claims (3) — REVISED based on experimental evidence\n17\t\n18\t1. **GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling is universal; pruning adds training collapse**: GRPO does not improve reasoning accuracy for ANY model post-SFT — unpruned (**81.27% = SFT 81.27%, Δ=0.00pp, identical 1072/1319 correct**), Standard-pruned (58.91% vs 59.29%, Δ=-0.38pp), RASP-pruned (60.65% vs 61.49%, Δ=-0.84pp). Reward increases dramatically (unpruned: 0→0.661) yet accuracy is unchanged — a universal reward-accuracy decoupling under GRPO+GSM8K+greedy. The pruning-specific phenomenon is **training collapse**: RASP collapses permanently at step ~10 (frac_zero_std→0.95, grad→0.007), Standard shows transient dip at step ~60, while unpruned trains stably for 100 steps. GRPO's reward signal does not encode genuine reasoning improvement; pruning removes the structural capacity to even sustain RL training.\n19\t\n20\t2. **Collapse severity gradient diagnoses structural damage**: Three-model comparison reveals a clean severity gradient — RASP (removes redundant, protects unique): permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039; Standard (importance-only): transient dip step ~60, final reward 0.065; Unpruned: no collapse, final reward 0.661. The 6× speedup from Standard→RASP confirms that functional redundancy provides RLVR exploration stability. Collapse dynamics are a zero-cost diagnostic: fast collapse = aggressive redundancy removal = poor RL trainability.\n21\t\n22\t3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning strategy**: For SFT recovery, RASP shows marginal advantage (+2.2pp, RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%, N=1319, p=0.25). For RLVR stability, RASP is actively harmful (6× faster collapse). The structures optimal to prune for SFT are exactly those needed for RLVR stability — a fundamental Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff. Consistent with \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" (ICLR 2026).\n23\t\n24\t## Evidence Status (as of 2026-05-16, ALL CORE DATA COMPLETE)\n25\t\n26\t| Evidence | Status | Result |\n27\t|----------|--------|--------|\n28\t| Unpruned SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 81.27% |\n29\t| Unpruned GRPO step-100 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **81.27% (Δ=0.00pp, 1072/1319 = identical to SFT)** |\n30\t| Unpruned GRPO step-90 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **80.59% (1063/1319, confirms stability across late training)** |\n31\t| Standard SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 59.29% |\n32\t| Standard GRPO step-50 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 58.91% (Δ=-0.38pp) |\n33\t| RASP SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 61.49% |\n34\t| RASP GRPO step-5 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 60.65% (Δ=-0.84pp) |\n35\t| RASP GRPO v9 collapse dynamics | ✅ | Permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039 |\n36\t| Standard GRPO v8 dynamics | ✅ | Transient dip step ~60, recovery step ~90 |\n37\t| Unpruned GRPO v2 dynamics | ✅ | No collapse, 100 steps stable, reward 0.661 |\n38\t| Alpha ablation (cal=512) | ✅ | U-shape: α≥1.0 > α≤0.5 post-prune |\n39\t| SFT gap significance | ⚠️ p=0.25 | Not significant at N=1319; scope expansion to higher sparsity planned |\n40\t| RASP GRPO step-10 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **61.87% — collapse onset does NOT reduce accuracy (vs step-5 60.65%, p=0.52)** |\n41\t\n42\t## Story Spine\n43\t\n44\t- **Problem**: The reasoning model compression pipeline (prune → recover → align) assumes alignment is independent of pruning decisions. We show this assumption fails catastrophically: GRPO alignment on pruned models produces reward improvement without accuracy gain, followed by complete collapse. The pruning-alignment interaction is not merely suboptimal — it is fundamentally broken under current practice.\n45\t\n46\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) claims RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression — but uses a single pruning ratio and does not report per-step accuracy during GRPO. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study recovery or alignment at all. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration without recovery. No work has documented GRPO collapse on pruned models, explained its mechanism, or shown that pruning strategy determines collapse dynamics.\n47\t\n48\t- **Our framing**: We present the first systematic study of how structural pruning interacts with RLVR alignment in reasoning LLMs. We introduce RASP (S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α) not as a universally superior method, but as a **diagnostic tool** that reveals the Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff: CKA-aware structure selection that benefits SFT recovery actively harms RLVR stability. This reframes the pruning-alignment relationship from \"which structures to remove for best recovery\" to \"recovery paradigm determines what counts as safe to remove.\"\n49\t\n50\t- **Headline result**: \"GRPO reward improvement never translates to accuracy gain (unpruned: reward 0→0.661, accuracy 81.27%→81.27%; identical 1072/1319 correct). But pruning causes GRPO training collapse: RASP-pruned collapses permanently at step 10, Standard-pruned at step 60, unpruned never. The severity gradient (RASP > Standard > Unpruned) reveals that structural redundancy — expendable for SFT — provides critical RL exploration stability.\"\n51\t\n52\t## Venue Fit\n53\t- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: structured pruning + reasoning model alignment failure analysis\n54\t- Negative/diagnostic results challenging published claims (Self-Healing) are high-impact at *ACL venues\n55\t- Reasoning model compression pipeline failures are immediately practical (timely: DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, Kimi-K1.5)\n56\t- Mechanistic analysis (collapse dynamics, reward-accuracy divergence) aligns with EMNLP empirical rigor\n57\t\n58\t## Venue Fit Risks\n59\t- **\"Just a negative result without solution\"**: Mitigate with (1) mechanistic explanation (redundancy-stability tradeoff), (2) RASP as diagnostic tool (collapse speed predicts pruning quality for RL), (3) actionable implication (SFT-only recovery is currently the safe path; RLVR needs pruning-aware modifications)\n60\t- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the canonical open reasoning model; multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard/Unpruned) + multi-recovery (SFT/GRPO) compensates\n61\t- **\"GRPO config might be wrong\"**: Report hyperparameter sensitivity (alpha ablation), show collapse is robust across configs, cite Self-Healing uses similar GRPO setup\n62\t- **\"SFT gap not significant\"**: Frame honestly as marginal; the paper's contribution is the GRPO failure + mechanism, not the SFT comparison. SFT gap is supplementary context.\n63\t- **\"Collapse might be training instability, not pruning-specific\"**: Unpruned GRPO ran 100 steps with zero collapse (reward 0.661, stable frac_zero_std ≤0.275) — pruning-specificity confirmed\n64\t\n65\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n66\t\n67\t| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n68\t|---------|----------|----------------------|\n69\t| GRPO failure might be hyperparameter issue | Alpha ablation shows U-shape is robust; reward increases but accuracy never follows | alpha_ablation_sweep |\n70\t| Need unpruned control for pruning-specificity | Unpruned GRPO: 100 steps stable, no collapse, reward 0.661 vs pruned collapse at step 10-60 | grpo_unpruned_v2 |\n71\t| SFT gap not significant | Acknowledged; paper's main claim is GRPO failure, not SFT superiority | sft_eval N=1319 |\n72\t| Collapse speed might not generalize | Multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard) + multi-config (alpha sweep) | grpo_v8, grpo_v9 |\n73\t| How does this relate to Self-Healing claims? | Self-Healing uses 25% unstructured; our structured pruning at 20% creates different damage pattern | Discussion section |\n74\t| What's the practical recommendation? | SFT recovery only for structurally pruned models; RLVR requires pruning-aware alignment (future work) | All experiments |\n75\t| CKA-aware pruning hurts RLVR — why publish RASP? | RASP is the diagnostic tool that REVEALS the tradeoff; its failure under RLVR is the evidence | grpo_v9 vs grpo_v8 |\n76\t\n77\t## Key Differentiations\n78\t- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: Claims RLVR recovers pruned models → we show GRPO fails (reward hacking + collapse); different pruning granularity and controlled collapse analysis\n79\t- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → we use intra-layer CKA as diagnostic tool revealing redundancy-stability tradeoff in reasoning LLMs\n80\t- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery/alignment study → we study the full prune-recover-align pipeline failure\n81\t- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → we study recovery paradigm interaction\n82\t- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → we show even optimal pruning STRUCTURE cannot save RLVR alignment\n83\t\n84\t## Open Questions (scope expansion experiments planned)\n85\t1. ~~Does unpruned model also show reward-accuracy divergence?~~ → YES, confirmed: 81.27% = 81.27%\n86\t2. ~~What do RASP v9 fine-grained checkpoints show?~~ → Permanent collapse, step-5 eval = 60.65% (≈ SFT)\n87\t3. Can higher sparsity (25-30%) make SFT gap significant AND intensify GRPO collapse? (scope expansion Phase 1)\n88\t4. Does the collapse pattern reproduce on Qwen2.5-Math-7B? (scope expansion Phase 2)\n89\t5. Is there a GRPO config that avoids collapse on pruned models? (future work motivation)\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c42f2d0-ce33-4817-aaea-db7e5633e350","uuid":"35839a62-92fb-4ce2-9ada-7ad6fc85f6e8","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:16:53.951Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n\n## Core Insight (Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff)\nRLVR alignment (GRPO) fundamentally fails on structurally pruned reasoning models: reward improves but accuracy does not — a pruning-induced reward hacking phenomenon. We show the failure mechanism via **collapse dynamics**: pruning method determines how fast GRPO collapses, and this speed is a diagnostic of structural damage type. Crucially, functional redundancy plays **opposite roles** under SFT vs RLVR recovery:\n\n- **SFT**: redundant structures (high CKA overlap) are safely removable — their function redistributes through gradient-based learning. CKA-aware pruning (RASP) yields marginal SFT advantage.\n- **RLVR**: redundant structures provide **exploration stability** — backup paths that prevent policy collapse during RL. Removing them (as RASP does) accelerates collapse.\n\nThis creates a **Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff**: the structures optimal to prune for SFT recovery are exactly those needed for RLVR stability. Optimal pruning is fundamentally conditioned on the recovery paradigm.\n\n## Core Claims (3) — REVISED based on experimental evidence\n\n1. **GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling is universal; pruning adds training collapse**: GRPO does not improve reasoning accuracy for ANY model post-SFT — unpruned (**81.27% = SFT 81.27%, Δ=0.00pp, identical 1072/1319 correct**), Standard-pruned (58.91% vs 59.29%, Δ=-0.38pp), RASP-pruned (60.65% vs 61.49%, Δ=-0.84pp). Reward increases dramatically (unpruned: 0→0.661) yet accuracy is unchanged — a universal reward-accuracy decoupling under GRPO+GSM8K+greedy. The pruning-specific phenomenon is **training collapse**: RASP collapses permanently at step ~10 (frac_zero_std→0.95, grad→0.007), Standard shows transient dip at step ~60, while unpruned trains stably for 100 steps. GRPO's reward signal does not encode genuine reasoning improvement; pruning removes the structural capacity to even sustain RL training.\n\n2. **Collapse severity gradient diagnoses structural damage**: Three-model comparison reveals a clean severity gradient — RASP (removes redundant, protects unique): permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039; Standard (importance-only): transient dip step ~60, final reward 0.065; Unpruned: no collapse, final reward 0.661. The 6× speedup from Standard→RASP confirms that functional redundancy provides RLVR exploration stability. Collapse dynamics are a zero-cost diagnostic: fast collapse = aggressive redundancy removal = poor RL trainability.\n\n3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning strategy**: For SFT recovery, RASP shows marginal advantage (+2.2pp, RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%, N=1319, p=0.25). For RLVR stability, RASP is actively harmful (6× faster collapse). The structures optimal to prune for SFT are exactly those needed for RLVR stability — a fundamental Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff. Consistent with \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" (ICLR 2026).\n\n## Evidence Status (as of 2026-05-16, ALL CORE DATA COMPLETE)\n\n| Evidence | Status | Result |\n|----------|--------|--------|\n| Unpruned SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 81.27% |\n| Unpruned GRPO step-100 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **81.27% (Δ=0.00pp, 1072/1319 = identical to SFT)** |\n| Unpruned GRPO step-90 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **80.59% (1063/1319, confirms stability across late training)** |\n| Standard SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 59.29% |\n| Standard GRPO step-50 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 58.91% (Δ=-0.38pp) |\n| RASP SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 61.49% |\n| RASP GRPO step-5 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 60.65% (Δ=-0.84pp) |\n| RASP GRPO v9 collapse dynamics | ✅ | Permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039 |\n| Standard GRPO v8 dynamics | ✅ | Transient dip step ~60, recovery step ~90 |\n| Unpruned GRPO v2 dynamics | ✅ | No collapse, 100 steps stable, reward 0.661 |\n| Alpha ablation (cal=512) | ✅ | U-shape: α≥1.0 > α≤0.5 post-prune |\n| SFT gap significance | ⚠️ p=0.25 | Not significant at N=1319; scope expansion to higher sparsity planned |\n| RASP GRPO step-10 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **61.87% — collapse onset does NOT reduce accuracy (vs step-5 60.65%, p=0.52)** |\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: The reasoning model compression pipeline (prune → recover → align) assumes alignment is independent of pruning decisions. We show this assumption fails catastrophically: GRPO alignment on pruned models produces reward improvement without accuracy gain, followed by complete collapse. The pruning-alignment interaction is not merely suboptimal — it is fundamentally broken under current practice.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) claims RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression — but uses a single pruning ratio and does not report per-step accuracy during GRPO. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study recovery or alignment at all. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration without recovery. No work has documented GRPO collapse on pruned models, explained its mechanism, or shown that pruning strategy determines collapse dynamics.\n\n- **Our framing**: We present the first systematic study of how structural pruning interacts with RLVR alignment in reasoning LLMs. We introduce RASP (S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α) not as a universally superior method, but as a **diagnostic tool** that reveals the Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff: CKA-aware structure selection that benefits SFT recovery actively harms RLVR stability. This reframes the pruning-alignment relationship from \"which structures to remove for best recovery\" to \"recovery paradigm determines what counts as safe to remove.\"\n\n- **Headline result**: \"GRPO reward improvement never translates to accuracy gain (unpruned: reward 0→0.661, accuracy 81.27%→81.27%; identical 1072/1319 correct). But pruning causes GRPO training collapse: RASP-pruned collapses permanently at step 10, Standard-pruned at step 60, unpruned never. The severity gradient (RASP > Standard > Unpruned) reveals that structural redundancy — expendable for SFT — provides critical RL exploration stability.\"\n\n## Venue Fit\n- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: structured pruning + reasoning model alignment failure analysis\n- Negative/diagnostic results challenging published claims (Self-Healing) are high-impact at *ACL venues\n- Reasoning model compression pipeline failures are immediately practical (timely: DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, Kimi-K1.5)\n- Mechanistic analysis (collapse dynamics, reward-accuracy divergence) aligns with EMNLP empirical rigor\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **\"Just a negative result without solution\"**: Mitigate with (1) mechanistic explanation (redundancy-stability tradeoff), (2) RASP as diagnostic tool (collapse speed predicts pruning quality for RL), (3) actionable implication (SFT-only recovery is currently the safe path; RLVR needs pruning-aware modifications)\n- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the canonical open reasoning model; multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard/Unpruned) + multi-recovery (SFT/GRPO) compensates\n- **\"GRPO config might be wrong\"**: Report hyperparameter sensitivity (alpha ablation), show collapse is robust across configs, cite Self-Healing uses similar GRPO setup\n- **\"SFT gap not significant\"**: Frame honestly as marginal; the paper's contribution is the GRPO failure + mechanism, not the SFT comparison. SFT gap is supplementary context.\n- **\"Collapse might be training instability, not pruning-specific\"**: Unpruned GRPO ran 100 steps with zero collapse (reward 0.661, stable frac_zero_std ≤0.275) — pruning-specificity confirmed\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n\n| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n|---------|----------|----------------------|\n| GRPO failure might be hyperparameter issue | Alpha ablation shows U-shape is robust; reward increases but accuracy never follows | alpha_ablation_sweep |\n| Need unpruned control for pruning-specificity | Unpruned GRPO: 100 steps stable, no collapse, reward 0.661 vs pruned collapse at step 10-60 | grpo_unpruned_v2 |\n| SFT gap not significant | Acknowledged; paper's main claim is GRPO failure, not SFT superiority | sft_eval N=1319 |\n| Collapse speed might not generalize | Multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard) + multi-config (alpha sweep) | grpo_v8, grpo_v9 |\n| How does this relate to Self-Healing claims? | Self-Healing uses 25% unstructured; our structured pruning at 20% creates different damage pattern | Discussion section |\n| What's the practical recommendation? | SFT recovery only for structurally pruned models; RLVR requires pruning-aware alignment (future work) | All experiments |\n| CKA-aware pruning hurts RLVR — why publish RASP? | RASP is the diagnostic tool that REVEALS the tradeoff; its failure under RLVR is the evidence | grpo_v9 vs grpo_v8 |\n\n## Key Differentiations\n- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: Claims RLVR recovers pruned models → we show GRPO fails (reward hacking + collapse); different pruning granularity and controlled collapse analysis\n- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → we use intra-layer CKA as diagnostic tool revealing redundancy-stability tradeoff in reasoning LLMs\n- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery/alignment study → we study the full prune-recover-align pipeline failure\n- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → we study recovery paradigm interaction\n- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → we show even optimal pruning STRUCTURE cannot save RLVR alignment\n\n## Open Questions (scope expansion experiments planned)\n1. ~~Does unpruned model also show reward-accuracy divergence?~~ → YES, confirmed: 81.27% = 81.27%\n2. ~~What do RASP v9 fine-grained checkpoints show?~~ → Permanent collapse, step-5 eval = 60.65% (≈ SFT)\n3. Can higher sparsity (25-30%) make SFT gap significant AND intensify GRPO collapse? (scope expansion Phase 1)\n4. Does the collapse pattern reproduce on Qwen2.5-Math-7B? (scope expansion Phase 2)\n5. Is there a GRPO config that avoids collapse on pruned models? (future work motivation)\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
